# ReferenceDataService: the cache of reads by key. Watch the X-Cache response header.

@server = http://localhost:5005/odata/v4/reference-data
@auth = Basic alice:alice


### X-Cache: MISS, then HIT on the second call (time to live 600 s, from the service)
GET {{server}}/CustomerGroups('G100')
Authorization: {{auth}}

###
GET {{server}}/CustomerGroups('G100')
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Two keys: MISS
GET {{server}}/CustomerNames?$filter=ID in ('C001','C002')
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Three keys, two cached: X-Cache: PARTIAL; hits=2; misses=1 (only C003 goes to the backend)
GET {{server}}/CustomerNames?$filter=ID in ('C001','C002','C003')
Authorization: {{auth}}

### The key read behind $expand is cached too: CustomerGroups('G300') is a HIT the second time
GET {{server}}/CustomerNames('C004')?$expand=_Group
Authorization: {{auth}}

### @remote.cache: false: never cached, no X-Cache header
GET {{server}}/Stock('P001')
Authorization: {{auth}}

### @remote.cache.ttl: 60 on the entity
GET {{server}}/Categories('ELEC')
Authorization: {{auth}}
